.TH MARBOR\-ROUTING 1 "2026-08-17" "marbor dev" "Marbor Manual"
.SH NAME
marbor\-routing \- manage routing rules and global routing strategy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B marbor routing
[action] [args] [\fIflags\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
manage routing rules and global routing strategy
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B rules
list/add/remove/toggle routing rules
.TP
.B rules list
list routing rules
.TP
.B rules add
add a routing rule
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-id string
rule id (required) (required)
.TP
.B \-\-condition string
match condition (required) (required)
.TP
.B \-\-target string
target node name
.TP
.B \-\-strategy string
per\-rule strategy override
.TP
.B \-\-priority int
rule priority (higher wins)
.TP
.B \-\-enabled
enable immediately
.RE
.TP
.B rules remove <id>
remove a routing rule
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-yes
confirm removal without prompting
.RE
.TP
.B rules toggle <id>
toggle a routing rule's enabled state
.TP
.B strategy
get/set the global routing strategy
.TP
.B strategy get
show the global routing strategy
.TP
.B strategy set <strategy>
set the global routing strategy
.SH FLAGS
.TP
.B \-\-server
Admin API base URL (default "http://localhost:8080", env MARBOR_SERVER)
.TP
.B \-\-json
output machine\-readable JSON instead of a human table
.TP
.B \-\-username
admin username, used to log in (env MARBOR_USERNAME)
.TP
.B \-\-password
admin password, used to log in (env MARBOR_PASSWORD)
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmarbor\fR(1)
